<title>UK: P&amp;O shares drop as UBS downgrades to &quot;hold&quot;.</title>
<headline>P&amp;O shares drop as UBS downgrades to &quot;hold&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Peninsular and Oriental Steam Navigation Co fell on Friday after analysts at UBS downgraded their recommendation on the stock to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;buy&quot;, traders said.</p>
<p>P&amp;O shares were 20-1/2p weaker at 621-1/2 by 0841 GMT on volume of 2.5 million shares.  </p>
<p>Market sources said UBS had cut its 1997 profit forecast for P&amp;O by 10 percent.</p>
<p>P&amp;O shares hit a three-month high of 649 earlier this week, helped by news that the transport and construction group had sold two of its shopping centre properties.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Marshall, London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
